   "answer": "The anchored deviation estimator used by Task-CoEvolve is defined as \\(\\hat{S}(h) = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t \\in T} \\bar{p}_t + \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t \\in S_k} \\frac{x_t(h) - \\bar{p}_t}{\\pi_t}\\), where \\(\\bar{p}_t\\) is the historical success rate of task \\(t\\) and \\(\\pi_t\\) is its sampling probability [3:15]. The raw outcome is not weighted directly because weighting the outcome \\(x_t(h)\\) by \\(1/\\pi_t\\) would cause instability when tasks have small \\(\\pi_t\\) and are consistently solved or failed, making their term dominate the estimate; instead, Task-CoEvolve weights the deviation from the anchor \\(\\bar{p}_t\\) to avoid this issue [3:15]."
  },
