   "answer": "On EPLB, the agent had plateaued at a score of ∼0.21 for over 120 turns. It diagnosed that the refinement phase was stuck because the code only allowed experts with two or more replicas to donate, too restrictive to resolve many imbalances. Temporarily allowing an expert to give up its last replica let refinement explore beneficial intermediate states it could never reach before. This single operator change broke the plateau, yielding the pivotal improvement that ultimately lifted the score from 0.21 to 0.23. [4:23]"
